<symbol type="16" id="145" code="522" name="Canopy"><description>A canopy is a building construction (with a roof), normally supported by pillars, poles or walls, such as passages, gangways, courts, bus stops, gas stations or garages.
Small passable parts of buildings which cannot easily be crossed by competitors, shall not be represented on the map and shall be closed during the competition.
Minimum width: 0.5 mm.
Minimum area: 0.25 mm² (footprint 4 m²).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part symbol="146"/><part symbol="147"/></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="4" id="146" code="522.3" name="Canopy, fill"><description>A canopy is a building construction (with a roof), normally supported by pillars, poles or walls, such as passages, gangways, courts, bus stops, gas stations or garages.
